Docker Compose HTTPD on App Server 1
Problem: On App Server 1 create a container named httpd using a docker compose file /opt/docker/docker-compose.yml. Use httpd image, map port 80 to 3001, map /usr/local/apache2/htdocs to /opt/security.

Solution:

bash
# Create directory
sudo mkdir -p /opt/docker
cd /opt/docker

# Create docker-compose.yml
sudo vi /opt/docker/docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.yml content:

yaml
services:
  httpd-service:
    image: httpd:latest
    container_name: httpd
    ports:
      - "3001:80"
    volumes:
      - /opt/security:/usr/local/apache2/htdocs
bash
# Start the container
sudo docker compose up -d

# Verify
sudo docker ps
curl http://localhost:3001
